            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis of acute abdominal pain using a three-stage classifier.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-27</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present paper deals with an application of a three-stage classifier based on a decision tree logic to the diagnosis of acute abdominal pain. On the basis of clinical information collected from a series of 476 patients suffering from abdominal pain of acute onset, the method of multistage classifier synthesis is presented. The results of classification accuracy using a modified version of k-nearest neighbours strategy for different features used at interior nodes of a tree are given.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
